```java
interface Config {
    int MAX_USERS = 100;        // implicitly public static final
    // int count;               // ILLEGAL: no instance fields, must be initialized
}

class Service implements Config {
    void show() {
        System.out.println(Config.MAX_USERS); // a shared constant
        // MAX_USERS = 50;       // ILLEGAL: final, cannot reassign
    }
}
```
*Every interface field is a constant; mutable per-object state lives in classes, not interfaces.*

```java
interface Readable  { String read(); }
interface Writable  { void write(String s); }

interface ReadWrite extends Readable, Writable { } // extends MULTIPLE

class File implements ReadWrite {        // must implement BOTH inherited methods
    public String read() { return "data"; }
    public void write(String s) { /* ... */ }
}
```
*`ReadWrite` combines both contracts; `File` must satisfy every inherited method.*

```java
interface Auditable { }              // marker: empty, just a tag

class Payment implements Auditable { } // tagged
class Note    { }                      // not tagged

void maybeAudit(Object o) {
    if (o instanceof Auditable) {      // runtime check on the tag
        System.out.println("auditing " + o.getClass().getSimpleName());
    }
}
// JDK does the same: ObjectOutputStream checks 'instanceof Serializable'.
```

```java
interface Drawable {                     // CAN-DO capability
    void draw();
    default void render() { draw(); }    // Java 8 default method
}
class Circle extends Shape implements Drawable {   // one class, one interface
    Circle(String c) { super(c); }
    double area() { return 0; }
    public void draw() { /* ... */ }
}
// A class can implement many: implements Drawable, Comparable<Circle>
```

```java
interface Flyer  { default String move() { return "fly"; } }
interface Swimmer { default String move() { return "swim"; } }

class Duck implements Flyer, Swimmer {     // many interfaces: OK
    @Override public String move() {        // resolve the default clash
        return Flyer.super.move() + "/" + Swimmer.super.move();
    }
}
// class Duck extends Bird, Fish { }       // NOT allowed: conflicting state
```

```java
interface Notifier { void send(String msg); } // capability
class EmailNotifier implements Notifier { public void send(String m) { } }
class SmsNotifier   implements Notifier { public void send(String m) { } }
// Caller depends on Notifier; swap implementations freely.
```

```java
abstract class Game {                 // one family, shared structure
    private int score;                // shared state
    public final void play() {        // template method
        start(); score = computeScore(); end();
    }
    abstract void start();            // subclasses fill the holes
    abstract int computeScore();
    void end() { System.out.println("score: " + score); } // shared concrete
}
```
*Combine them when useful: an abstract base can implement an interface to provide a partial, reusable implementation.*
